# Testing core rules
Design docs live in testing/docs/cursor/ (arch-*.md, cat-*.md): read only those the task attaches. Service facts: testing/docs/SUT_MAP.md, read before touching a service; never re-read the whole repo. Style: python-style.mdc. UI: playwright.mdc. Prod edits: testing-modify-prod.mdc.

## Scope
- Write only in: testing/, .github/workflows/, infra/docker-compose.test.yml, root Makefile (include testing/testing.mk). nginx is never changed or relaxed.
- Prod code: only testability seams (testing-modify-prod.mdc). Never fix bugs or change behaviour: behaviour contradicting the documented spec = xfail(strict=True, reason="BUG-n: ...") + a line in testing/KNOWN_ISSUES.md; unspecified behaviour = pin with a `# characterization` comment.
- Ignore Datadog everywhere (will be removed).
- Characterise first (read the route, call it), then assert. Never invent endpoints, fields or status codes; if SUT_MAP lacks it, read that one file.
- One task per chat; stop when the task's DoD is green. Report <= 10 lines, no re-printing files; on failure show only the last 40 lines.
- Time-box: stuck >30 min on a workaround, or 3 failed fixes -> stop, take the fallback from arch-quality.md (risks) or report.

## Layers (never mix)
Markers come from the directory via root conftest; --strict-markers is on. Extra markers: slow, chaos, db, redis, kafka, serial, smoke (tests/smoke only), synthetic, critical (fast UI subset), clean_db.
- tests/unit: pure code, pytest-mock. Service unit tests are out of scope until the refactoring phase and go to services/<svc>/tests/unit.
- tests/contract/{http,events}: in-process, PG; OpenAPI validator, Schemathesis, Pydantic, snapshots.
- tests/component/<service>: in-process ASGI, one service, real PG + Redis + Redpanda; httpx.ASGITransport, respx, mocker.patch.
- tests/integration/{services,scenarios}: compose stack; network httpx; Kafka/Redis/MailHog/WireMock clients.
- tests/e2e_ui: compose stack; sync Playwright.
- tests/smoke: fresh stack/staging/prod URL, httpx, broad, blocks the pipeline.
- tests/synthetic/{api,browser}: prod/staging URL, narrow, alerts (never blocks). Policy: cat-smoke-synthetic.md.
- Component/contract: one service per pytest session (controller + its xdist workers, all OS processes): --service <name> (all services are packages named app).

## Test bodies
- Business-language steps via Flows / Page Objects only. No URLs, headers, SQL, locators or raw JSON in test bodies. The assertion about the behaviour under test stays visible in the test body (flows return ApiResponse); precondition steps (new_task) may assert inside flows.
- Adapters (HttpTaskApi, HttpAuthApi, KafkaEventReader) are concrete classes; Protocol only with >= 2 implementations (python-style.mdc). The same Flow runs at component and integration: only the injected httpx.AsyncClient transport differs. Dependency failures: mocker.patch(autospec=True).
- Names: test_<behaviour>_<condition>_<expected>; one behaviour per test; parametrize instead of copy-paste.

## Data and isolation
- All data is unique via RunContext(run_id, test_id) (unique_title()). Never assert on totals/emptiness of shared collections (e.g. GET /tasks); assert on own ids.
- Component: DB per xdist worker from a migrated template DB, real commits; the app builds its own engine from env (no get_db override). Redis: one DB index per worker (env), FLUSHDB before each test. Kafka: real Redpanda, unique ids, fresh consumer group (unique group_id), subscribe before producing, filter by own correlation id.
- Default = no DB cleanup. Tests asserting global state use @pytest.mark.clean_db (truncates only tables touched since last cleanup, before the test body).
- Integration/UI: no cleanup/reset; own data by uuid; seeded users read-only. Login and seed once per run (FileLock, token file with expiry check), never per test. Nginx /auth/ allows 5 req/min: functional tests use the gateway port; real nginx only for UI and edge tests. WireMock stubs match the test's own payload.id.
- Factories: Polyfactory (Faker bundled), all layers. .build() = no I/O; await .create_async() = DB rows via per-test bound __async_session__ (the rows fixture); .create_sync() = sync seeding (FileLock) or sync setup against the stack. Bind the session via a per-test subclass, never a mutable shared class attribute or ContextVar. Override business-constrained fields explicitly; Factory.seed_random(run_seed). Cache one argon2 hash, never hash per test.
- Tests are order-independent and parallel-safe (pytest-randomly + xdist). Heavy shared resources are session-scoped and created by the xdist controller only.

## Fixtures, async, mocking
- Scopes: infra = session; engine/clients = session (per worker); db session/app overrides = function. Always yield + cleanup; always dependency_overrides.clear() in teardown.
- pytest-asyncio: asyncio_mode="auto"; default fixture AND test loop scope = session.
- No TestClient with async DB: httpx.AsyncClient(transport=ASGITransport(app)). ASGITransport does not run lifespan: enter app.router.lifespan_context(app) in a session fixture.
- respx = intercept our outgoing httpx calls in-process. WireMock = real network stub for scripted sequences (503,503,200), timeouts, request journal. Never both for the same call.
- Eventual consistency: await eventually(fn, timeout=..., interval=..., message=...). No sleeps.
- Retry/backoff tests: patch asyncio.sleep and jitter; assert the call sequence, not wall-clock time.

## Quality gates (before "done")
ruff check, ruff format --check, pyright (strict on src/saas_testkit/), pytest <layer> -q pass; no unknown-marker warnings; tests pass 3x in a row, random order, -n auto. After tests for a service: break one prod line (or flip one assertion), confirm a test goes red, revert.
